WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.357
Fallback is a policy decision.

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:09.187
If the preferred source fails, the workflow should not automatically search anywhere it can find.

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:15.100
Fallbacks should be ordered by authority, permission, freshness, and cost.

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:21.214
For a structured order fact, an internal S Q L system may be the first source.

00:00:21.214 --> 00:00:27.194
If live external data is required, an approved A P I may be next.

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:34.119
Public web search should be used only when the application explicitly allows public evidence for the task.

00:00:34.119 --> 00:00:37.854
If no approved source can answer, stop safely.

00:00:38.344 --> 00:00:44.161
Never silently replace an authoritative internal policy source with public web results.

00:00:44.161 --> 00:00:51.276
Those sources may have different rules, different dates, or may refer to another organization entirely.
